      ":question/problem": "![](images/34/34f06c065f918c0559b1a1a3ff598a67b1dd4555147a3a98d7340cbfa9fe6bac.png)\n\nTriangles $ABC$ and $DEF$ each have a corresponding angle measuring $50^{\u2218}$. Which of the following additional pieces of information is sufficient to determine whether these triangles are similar?\n\n1. The length of line segment $AC^(\u2015)$.\n2. The measure of another pair of corresponding angles in the two triangles.\n3. The lengths of one pair of corresponding sides in the two triangles.\n4. No additional information is needed."
